From: EglantinePS5 <Vampinity@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: up: early read trace, what the game read against what landed later (EDEN_UP_EARLY_READ_TRACE, log only)

DRAFT, not built. Our own work (guard-door job). Log only. EDEN_UP_EARLY_READ_TRACE=1 (exact 1,
read once at boot, Common::PeSwitch; not a live switch); off by default. On: "ER r" lines for
reads that take guest memory as it is (present, ahead flag, 4 floats), "ER l" when a download
later lands over such a range (old/new values, after_us), "ER s"/"ER L" for landings, and a 10 s
counter line. At every present it bumps the read trap generation so each core's next read is
looked up again. Cost on: about LANDING_TRACE's 2 fps plus the lookups (lookup_us).
New file video_core/early_read_trace.h.

Reviewed draft (verdict "ready with corrections"): early-read-trace.v2.patch. Re-anchored after
0567 in gpu.cpp (OnCPURead: the note sits after AHEAD_READ_SYNC's test, before the shortcut's
return) and nx2_gsv.h (after LandingTrace, before AHEAD_READ_SYNC's block); all +/- lines
byte-identical to the v2.
